{"type":"message","id":"7ee79e40","parentId":"c6d07d26","timestamp":"2026-03-17T09:40:20.736Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_05d97e88d5148a470169b9217c827c8191a639f57b0aaf1b95\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"encrypted_content\":\"gAAAAABpuSF9d_WEq-yAbx8bqdoI7e6Of0bxqvdPH1SlCK4RwjzpbZNCx-nFI80siGcqcnEoGFqzifEGXQgTK-JcPF51FcuoTJ6CY-8qUZEY2EdKo61whFVjf14L8kUdHyHc0aY3dWAmhgbe68UIdALM8lHCcCYqXzyEif3NiI43trVrihwR0N_eHFBMrMxmHQs-OjvzHRbnCuyc4ZdGQvjOjS8EAYBT75BUNrCwVlcSKexw247Yc86WQg2CWm7lhWNCxgHM9RZ3ayvVaS70Iee9_SdWhR7DZlv768eqeaFP3LKBETDNTQSgtZZuP8VsPslfPVCDbaEbTZvcwEkjO69dI0WRbiqB5jQhTgugpW5WP-lOCu8uuo5PTlEPIKJolM7g3f5rlUmUL9ufnOViqt1g9zm5LCKiVzq5WtLM8fXNpJ10H2th8EbWxwpzVAMgO4SFba2F6ChenmUWPG_scx_kzszODrtNkjCNDDM3sWbr-tHZhlz5S-zfr_lFHheC1P361jf2lTUIjU9nS6NJA6hoMkzs_nMeVs-hgpJnX-mzabYGBd3rim3npXjyQjDKepKLl51Zg8d4fq0B7kVtUtIjByI9li2YMWhqTfFsEq7GTjl2Z1BAevja60y1rNpXopj_F-qVtgNKv8_I8x28tOaree05pTUfVn4FpVnCmuo0vA9WjZc9u6rvGMk9ONhnekfaBodwThN55GQRLIjxiyQ4FvcQXkRtiiV0Z9vXsjHe2jJ9MJWJHfbzy8DD8MPtGV-lZD9PG1pJpmKDk3p1iilFV_xb3-AgztudKVaQ-OS3ABywYP67ArSyW36uI5PXOQnLCRgwNoZD0yD2dMgXpc4W8D_hZFM7gBY1mi2Kmyl4Kin1ax0N_OZo855r7NKyORXHfOHNIn6f\",\"summary\":[]}"},{"type":"text","text":"[[reply_to_current]] I ran the kidney imaging pipeline on your CT scan.\n\n### Kidney pipeline summary\n- **Kidney cancer class:** **kidney_tumor**\n- **Confidence:** **99.998%**\n- **Image Analyzer prediction:** **kidney_tumor**\n\n### CAM findings\n- **CAM coverage:** **0.0128**\n- **CAM center ratio:** **0.825**\n- **CAM left-right asymmetry:** **0.10**\n- **CAM top-bottom asymmetry:** **1.00**\n- **CAM explanation:** the model focused on a **localized central region within the renal tissue** with an **asymmetric spatial pattern**, which the analyzer says is compatible with a **localized structural abnormality** in a tumor-prediction context.\n\n### What this means\n- This pipeline output is **concerning** and it is **consistent with a tumor signal** on the uploaded CT image.\n- It also fits with the broader clinical picture you’ve described: **pink urine, fatigue, weight loss, worsening right-sided pain**, and your prior kidney cancer history.\n\n### Important caution\n- This is still a **prototype imaging result**, **not a diagnosis by itself**.\n- But given the **very high model confidence** and your symptoms/history, I would treat this as something that needs **prompt specialist review**, ideally with your **urology/oncology team as soon as possible**.\n\n### What to do next\n- Please arrange **urgent review** with your treating team and share:\n  - the CT scan/report\n  - recent **urinalysis**\n  - **CBC**\n  - **creatinine/eGFR**\n- If you develop **heavy bleeding, clots, inability to urinate, severe worsening pain, fever, dizziness, chest pain, or shortness of breath**, seek urgent in-person care immediately.\n\nIf you want, I can next help you with either:\n1. a **plain-English interpretation** of this result in the context of your EHR/DNA, or  \n2. a **short message to send your oncologist/urologist today**.","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_05d97e88d5148a470169b9217d03c081918502ea4c21361af6\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":9198,"output":451,"cacheRead":50688,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":60337,"cost":{"input":0.022995,"output":0.006765,"cacheRead":0.012672,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.042432}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1773740410538}}
